A||N||5||Formula88||Help - Transmision Shop Suggestions||||8||
Z||000000||Formula88||02-28-2001||09:38 PM||||Ok, I don't really want to crack the case on my Getrag, and I'm not having much luck getting the input shaft bearing out otherwise.  I don't want to take a chance on screwing up something expensive.  So, here's the question.  Can anyone recommend a good transmission shop that will put the input shaft bearing in my Getrag if I bring it and the part to them?  It's already out of the car, so the bulk of the labor is done.  I'm in Raleigh, NC, but will travel if necessary to find a good, reliable shop.  I don't trust any of the shops in this area, unless someone can give me a good reference on one.  Any help is appreciated.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Rodney||02-28-2001||10:19 PM||||Anyone can split the case on a Getrag. It is very easy. Instructions are on my web page. Any machine type shop can install (press in/out) the new bearing. It is easy to put back it all back together. Why trust someone that may have no clue as to what to do?? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||02-28-2001||10:24 PM||||Thanks, Rodney.  I guess I'm just paranoid since I've never been inside a tranny before.  I did manage to get the tranny out of the car with LZeitgeist's help, so maybe we can get the bearing done, too.  I do know a machine shop that can do the bearing.  I've just been hesitant to crack the case.||||reg||1
Z||000003||PJ||03-02-2001||10:43 PM||||Rodney is correct. Nine out of ten shops won't know how to shim the diff bearings after changing them. Hang on, I sent you the factory manual pages.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Archie||03-02-2001||11:31 PM||||Go ahead & do it..... I did it with Rodneys instructions and now I feel like a pro.<P>BTW, just a few days ago I found a professional assembly manual for the Fiero Getrag at a swap meet..... pretty cool book. I told the magazine guy who had it to try to get a few more of them.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||03-03-2001||02:23 AM||||Now THAT sounds like a book I need to read!  Sooner or later I'm gonna have to rebuild this tranny.  Rebuilding an engine isn't a big deal, but the tranny is new territory.  Gotta learn sometime!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
